bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28, 0, "form_control_label_width_milli_px, k > 1 branch: resolve_font_metrics_with_language_milli(family, label, num * 1000 * k / den) is called before the FORM_CONTROL_MEASURE_MAX_PX cap that bounds the oversampled k = 1 measurement. A large authored control font at a high device scale (e.g. font-size:200px at k = 4 = 800 px) is measured uncapped; the milli resolver itself falls back to the whole-px path above 512 px and uses a reference size of 8 x px capped at 512, so precision and cost at large sizes are unverified."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28, P3, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "web render: device-scale button label width path skips the FORM_CONTROL_MEASURE_MAX_PX cap", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_foundation.spl, 1004, "<button style=font-size:200px>Go</button> at device scale 4; inspect the size passed to resolve_font_metrics_with_language_milli", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 tabbar lane: found in review, not reproduced. Either apply the cap (fall back to the oversampled path above it) or document why the milli resolver's own 512 px limits make it unnecessary."
    web_render_button_device_label_width_skips_measure_cap_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 button-label-cluster lane: reproduced. Chrome 159: <button style=font-size:200px;padding:4px>Go</button> is 276.7969 CSS px at k=1 AND k=4 (label 266.7969, 1067.19 device px; right border column 1103 at k=4). Simple drew 1104 (4 x 277): above the cap the oversample fell to 2x (400 px) and rounded the run to a whole 267 px, so button_device_extra_w was 0. Fix (_measure_button_label_width_milli, layout_foundation.spl): a capped oversample (over < 12, incl. a font > 512 px now measured at its own size instead of returning the whole-px fallback) takes the run's exact width_milli as a LayoutUnit of a device px. Red->green: test/01_unit/browser_engine/button_input_device_width_chrome159_spec.spl AC-1 (base 2bc96bcf7de FAIL k=4 'borders 0 1104', lane PASS). Separate defect found, filed as web_render_glyph_run_over_512_device_px_not_painted_2026-11-28: the label glyphs are painted capped (ink 21..649 vs Chrome 60..1053 at k=4)."

